{
 "_doc": "Overworld figures per era (docs/ERA_FEEL_CHARS.md): the Wayfarer, villagers, Tamers and the Spirling that walks behind. Read by scripts/overworld/EraActorLook.gd; the sheets come from tools/art/gen_era_chars.py. One entry per era I-V and every era sets every key in EraActorLook.KEYS. Era I and II keep the 64x32 sheets in art/eraN/chars (sheet_dir chars, drawn by GridWalker as before); from Era III the sheets live in art/eraN/actors and EraActorLook draws them. A later era never drops a feature: switches stay on, numbers only grow (step_px only shrinks), lists only get longer. frame: sprite size in px. colours: 4 = four tones per figure, more = zone colours with shading. rows: sheet row of each pose (4 columns: down, up, left, right). step_seq: poses of one tile step in order (stand, half, step); the foot alternates per tile. step_px: the figure moves in jumps of this many px (2 = coarse tile-by-tile slide, 1 = every pixel). walk_time/run_time: seconds per tile, read only by the test that pins them to GridWalker (running exists from Era I, hold the cancel key). run_anim: own running poses. ride: own pose on the reed float for crossings with ride_gear. shadow: none or drop. emotes: bubble kinds the era can show; emote_style: ink (the old ink box and label), flat, tail, shadow, live; emote_frames: frames per bubble; emote_pop: bubble pops in. emote_on: what shows which bubble (spot = a Tamer sees you, talk = talked to, talk_beaten = a beaten Tamer talked to, near/near_night/near_rain = a villager notices you, follower = you turn to your Spirling). head_turn: villagers turn their head to the Wayfarer within head_turn_radius tiles. follower: ink (still ink shadow, jumps a tile) or colour (own colours); follower_glide: it walks the tile and hops; follower_shadow. idle: still or breathe_blink. turn_blend: a quarter turn shows a head-first frame. outfits: none or season (columns blocks of the sheet in the order of seasons).",
